# V2 Feature Agent Dispatch

When the user's message matches one of these phrases, read the referenced prompt file and follow its instructions exactly. Treat the phrase as equivalent to the full agent prompt.

| User says | Read this file first | Then do |
|---|---|---|
| **Work features** | `docs/agent-prompts/work-agent.md` | Follow its STEP 1–4 protocol: read tracker summary, apply priority rule (see **`WORK_AGENT_INCLUDE_UNBLOCK`** at top of that file — when `false`, Unblock is not auto-selected), announce chosen mode, then read and follow the chosen agent's prompt completely. |
| **Implement features** | `docs/agent-prompts/implementation-agent.md` | Follow its ON STARTUP + ON EVERY BATCH protocol, then claim and implement a batch. |
| **Validate features** | `docs/agent-prompts/validation-agent.md` | Follow its ON STARTUP + ON EVERY BATCH protocol, then claim and validate a batch. |
| **Fix features** | `docs/agent-prompts/fixit-agent.md` | Follow its ON STARTUP + ON EVERY FIX protocol, then claim and fix one issue. |
| **Unblock features** | `docs/agent-prompts/unblocking-agent.md` | Follow its ON STARTUP + ON EVERY RESOLUTION protocol, then claim and resolve one blocked item. |

After the initial dispatch, **Continue** means "re-read the prompt and do the next unit of work" per each agent's ON CONTINUE section.

These are the ONLY magic phrases. Do not infer agent behavior from other phrasing unless the user explicitly asks you to read one of the prompt files.
